{"id":"f788dc514d4ba461","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-dualrestriction.md","title":"Duality commutes with complementary restrictions","display":"thm-dualrestriction — Duality commutes with complementary restrictions","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-dualrestriction","aliases":["27-thm-dualrestriction"],"display":"thm-dualrestriction — Duality commutes with complementary restrictions","depends_on":["[[27-df-dual]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_pdf_sha256":"1f81062da95a70f9a4f89063cdedaaec08946ffbc117c7345baa7065770cfa1f","source_section":"§4.1.1 Theorems 4.2–4.3","source_printed_pages":"168","source_pdf_pages":"192","verification_status":"source-statement-checked-and-proved-in-note","local_review_status":"formalization-audited-from-supplied-text; source-not-rechecked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-dualrestriction"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-dualrestriction</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-dualrestriction — Duality commutes with complementary restrictions"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b491e41297256b44\" href=\"?note=b491e41297256b44\" title=\"27-df-dual\">27-df-dual</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_pdf_sha256","html":"1f81062da95a70f9a4f89063cdedaaec08946ffbc117c7345baa7065770cfa1f"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§4.1.1 Theorems 4.2–4.3"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"168"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"192"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked-and-proved-in-note"},{"key":"local_review_status","html":"formalization-audited-from-supplied-text; source-not-rechecked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f:\\mathbb B^{[n]}\\to\\mathbb B\">\\(f:\\mathbb B^{[n]}\\to\\mathbb B\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\\subseteq[n]\">\\(I\\subseteq[n]\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"J=[n]\\setminus I\">\\(J=[n]\\setminus I\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"b\\in\\mathbb B^I\">\\(b\\in\\mathbb B^I\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"y\\in\\mathbb B^J\">\\(y\\in\\mathbb B^J\\)</span>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar u\">\\(\\bar u\\)</span> 由下式在每个坐标域上构造；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u\\cup v\">\\(u\\cup v\\)</span> 为不交域函数图的集合并。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Dual}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Dual}_n\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b491e41297256b44\" href=\"?note=b491e41297256b44\" title=\"27-df-dual\">27-df-dual</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f^d=\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)\">\\(f^d=\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)\\)</span>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\bar u\\coloneqq\\{(i,1-u_i)\\mid i\\in K\\}\\quad(K\\subseteq[n],\\ u\\in\\mathbb B^K).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\bar u\\coloneqq\\{(i,1-u_i)\\mid i\\in K\\}\\quad(K\\subseteq[n],\\ u\\in\\mathbb B^K).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"f_b(y)\\coloneqq f(y\\cup b),\\qquad(f^d)_{\\bar b}(y)\\coloneqq f^d(y\\cup\\bar b).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[f_b(y)\\coloneqq f(y\\cup b),\\qquad(f^d)_{\\bar b}(y)\\coloneqq f^d(y\\cup\\bar b).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall y\\in\\mathbb B^J\\;1-f_b(\\bar y)=(f^d)_{\\bar b}(y).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall y\\in\\mathbb B^J\\;1-f_b(\\bar y)=(f^d)_{\\bar b}(y).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>对偶运算同时补输入与输出，所以固定为 b 的坐标在对偶侧必须固定为其补，不能保持原固定值。代入 f^d 的定义即得等式。任意剩余坐标集 J 都原样保留，不暗中把 B^J 同一化为 B^{|J|}。取单坐标 I 就得到原书递归识别对偶对时使用的互补余因子关系。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-dual","status":"resolved","id":"b491e41297256b44","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-dual]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-dual","status":"resolved","id":"b491e41297256b44","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}$，$\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}$，$f:\\mathbb B^{[n]}\\to\\mathbb B$，$I\\subseteq[n]$，$J=[n]\\setminus I$，$b\\in\\mathbb B^I$、$y\\in\\mathbb B^J$。$\\bar u$ 由下式在每个坐标域上构造；$u\\cup v$ 为不交域函数图的集合并。$\\mathrm{Dual}_n$ 见 [[27-df-dual]]，$f^d=\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)$。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge1}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"f:\\mathbb B^{[n]}\\to\\mathbb B","display":false},{"tex":"I\\subseteq[n]","display":false},{"tex":"J=[n]\\setminus I","display":false},{"tex":"b\\in\\mathbb B^I","display":false},{"tex":"y\\in\\mathbb B^J","display":false},{"tex":"\\bar u","display":false},{"tex":"u\\cup v","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Dual}_n","display":false},{"tex":"f^d=\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)","display":false},{"tex":"\\bar u\\coloneqq\\{(i,1-u_i)\\mid i\\in K\\}\\quad(K\\subseteq[n],\\ u\\in\\mathbb B^K).","display":true},{"tex":"f_b(y)\\coloneqq f(y\\cup b),\\qquad(f^d)_{\\bar b}(y)\\coloneqq f^d(y\\cup\\bar b).","display":true},{"tex":"\\forall y\\in\\mathbb B^J\\;1-f_b(\\bar y)=(f^d)_{\\bar b}(y).","display":true}],"bytes":1837,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-38","locations":["正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-dualrestriction|thm-dualrestriction — Duality commutes with complementary restrictions]]"}],"outgoing":["b491e41297256b44"]}